<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Volksraad (Dutch East Indies)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1918–1942</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Volksraad (People's Council) was an advisory and later partly legislative assembly of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-indies">Dutch East Indies</a>, which first met in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/batavia">Batavia</a> in 1918. Its members were partly elected by local councils and partly appointed, and included Indonesians, Europeans, and Chinese and Arab residents. It gave Indonesian nationalists a public forum but had little real power, and it ceased to function after the Japanese invasion of 1942.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/volksraad-dutch-east-indies.jpg" alt="Volksraad (Dutch East Indies)" width="320" height="252" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sodacan · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:State_coat_of_arms_of_the_Netherlands.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
